title: Generals of the Republic
subtitle: Should the Jedi lead the Republic's armies?
tags: event
view-if: war and geonosis_seen and not war_begins_seen
max-visits: 1
priority: 4
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_war.svg
on-arrival: war_begins_seen = 1

= Generals of the Republic

[? if clones > 0 : The Grand Army needs commanders, and the clones were bred to follow Jedi. ?][? if clones <= 0 : The Republic's patchwork forces need commanders. ?] [? if not jedi_service_act : [? if rc_chancellor : The Security Bloc proposes?][? if not rc_chancellor : The Chancellor proposes?] that Jedi Knights be commissioned as generals. Many Jedi are uneasy: they are keepers of the peace, not soldiers. ?][? if jedi_service_act : But the Jedi Service Act forbids it: the Jedi may never hold military command. [? if rc_chancellor : The Security Bloc moves?][? if not rc_chancellor : The Chancellor moves?] that the Senate suspend the Act for the duration of the war, so that Jedi Knights can be commissioned as generals. Many Jedi quietly hope the motion fails. ?]

- @generals: Accept Jedi as generals.
- @advisors: Insist that the Jedi serve as advisors and peacekeepers, not commanders.
- @defend: Defend the Jedi Service Act.
- @suspend: Let the Act be suspended.

@generals
view-if: not jedi_service_act
subtitle: The war will go better. The Order will pay a heavy price.
on-arrival: jedi_generals = 1; war_balance += 1

The Jedi become generals. Within a year, a tenth of the Order has died in battle, and the public begins to see the Jedi as soldiers.

@advisors
view-if: not jedi_service_act
subtitle: The Order stays itself. The war will be harder.
on-arrival: jedi_generals = 0; war_balance -= 1; jedi_relation += 8; jedi_standing += 3; rad_hawk += 4

The Senate keeps the Jedi out of the chain of command. They serve as negotiators, scouts and protectors of civilians. The Order is grateful. The Security Bloc is not.

@defend
view-if: jedi_service_act
subtitle: The Caucus votes against the motion. If the Act holds, the Order stays itself and the war is harder.
on-arrival: {!
// blocs friendly to the Caucus side with it in keeping the Act; the vote is on suspending it
var keep = SW.stance(Q, {pal: 0.05, sec: 0.1, guild: 0.4, mod: 0.55 - Q.fear / 300, ind: 0.65, rim: 0.65, rfc: 0.7, cis: 1}, true);
var st = {};
for (var b in keep) st[b] = 1 - keep[b];
Q.ws_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 0, 'army');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Suspension of the Jedi Service Act', Q.ws_vote);
if (Q.ws_vote >= 50) { Q.ws_held = 0; SW.suspendServiceAct(Q); }
else { Q.ws_held = 1; Q.jedi_generals = 0; Q.war_balance -= 1; Q.jedi_relation += 8; Q.jedi_standing += 3; Q.rad_hawk += 4; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if ws_held : The Act holds. The Jedi stay out of the chain of command, and serve as negotiators, scouts and protectors of civilians. The Order is grateful. The Security Bloc is not. ?][? if not ws_held : The Act is suspended for the duration of the war. The Jedi become generals. Within a year, a tenth of the Order has died in battle, and the public begins to see the Jedi as soldiers. ?]

@suspend
view-if: jedi_service_act
subtitle: The war will go better. The Order will pay a heavy price, and it will remember who let it happen.
on-arrival: {! SW.suspendServiceAct(Q); Q.jedi_relation -= 6; Q.rad_hawk -= 2; !}

The Caucus lets the motion pass without a fight. The Act is suspended for the duration of the war, and the Jedi become generals. The Council does not say anything in public. In private, Master Windu says a great deal.
